2.25	2	VC2	VC Firm 2
Explanation: VC2 funded two startups averaging (2.5 + 2) / 2 = 2.25, strictly above its 2.00 limit, so it qualifies. VC1's average of 1.5 only equals its 1.5 limit and is excluded, as is any firm whose average does not strictly exceed its ceiling or that funded fewer than 2 startups; among qualifiers, only the firm with the highest avg_funding is returned. The fs_funded_startups table contains more rows than sampled above; the output is computed over the full dataset.

Constraints
Firms with no funded startups can never qualify (they have no average check size and fewer than 2 deals). A startup whose funding amount is undisclosed (NULL) still counts toward the minimum-deal threshold but must not contribute to the average.

Firms with no funded startups never qualify

A firm qualifies only if its average funding is strictly greater than its funding_limit (equal does not qualify)

A firm qualifies only if it has funded at least 2 startups

avg_funding and funding_limit must be reported to 2 decimal places

Output columns must be exactly avg_funding, funding_limit, vc_id, vc_name

Sort qualifying firms by avg_funding in descending order and return only the top 1 row
